🚀 Summary:
Today, I completed a hands-on lab where I set up a Jenkins pipeline to automate the deployment of a Dockerized application on Amazon EKS. I used eksctl to create the EKS cluster, configured access with kubectl, and integrated Jenkins with AWS for seamless CI/CD automation. This lab enhanced my understanding of Kubernetes cluster management and secure application deployment in the cloud.

🔧 Tools Used:

Jenkins: Configured a multi-branch pipeline for CI/CD.

eksctl: Used to create and manage the Amazon EKS cluster.

AWS CLI & kubectl: Managed cluster configurations and deployments.

💡 Skills Gained:

CI/CD Automation: Built an automated Jenkins pipeline for Kubernetes deployments.

Kubernetes Management: Created and managed EKS clusters with eksctl and kubectl.

Secure AWS Integration: Configured AWS credentials securely in Jenkins.

🚀 Challenges Faced:

Configuring Kubernetes access for Jenkins due to permission errors.

Setting up AWS IAM authentication for secure cluster access.

✅ Why It Matters:
This lab demonstrates practical skills in cloud-native CI/CD automation with Jenkins and Amazon EKS, essential for modern DevOps and cloud infrastructure roles. Mastering these tools allows for efficient, scalable, and secure application deployment.

